  "identity": "GW Human tribal midrange that wins by out-sizing rather than out-numbering. Sixteen of the seventeen creature cards are Humans, and Metallic Mimic naming Human makes every one of them that arrives afterwards enter carrying a permanent +1/+1 counter; Mayor of Avabruck adds a static, retroactive +1/+1 on top. Hamlet Captain and Intrepid Provisioner turn that base into combat swings, Butcher's Cleaver reads 'as long as equipped creature is a Human, it has lifelink', and Thalia, Heretic Cathar taxes every opposing deployment while the deck deploys ahead of it. Where the aggro Torens build spends its cards on board count, this one spends them on card advantage - Thraben Inspector, Duskwatch Recruiter, Tireless Tracker and Ulvenwald Mysteries all convert lands, spare mana and dead bodies into cards - and on six creature-answering spells plus Faith Unbroken's exile, so it can trade one-for-one all game and still be the deck with the larger board on turn seven.",
